    {
      "id": "ledger-notes",
      "kind": {
        "text": "PROVED HERE AS OF 2026-08-14; it was `open` in this ledger the same morning, and `external_status: proved` was always right -- this is a standard first-order validity, so the gap was import, not discovery. WHAT WAS MISSING, and why the one-line diagnosis on the earlier note was half right. The note predicted a single structural rule, `not (forall x . phi) -> exists x . not phi`. That rule was necessary and is now `quant.negation_duality.v1`, but it is NOT sufficient, and the reason is a property of this IR rather than of the mathematics: the SMT-LIB parser gives every binder occurrence a fresh arena symbol, so the four `x`s in the benchmark are four distinct symbols `!q.x.0 .. !q.x.3`. Pushing the negation inward turns the first conjunct into `(= (exists !q.x.0 . not (P !q.x.0)) (exists !q.x.1 . not (P !q.x.1)))` -- alpha-equivalent, hash-consed apart, and invisible to equality reflexivity. Closing the fact needed a second capability, alpha-equivalence of quantified terms (`eq.alpha_equivalent.v1`), which did not exist anywhere in the tree. SOUNDNESS. The duality rewrite performs no substitution -- it flips the operator and wraps the body in one `not`, leaving the body byte-identical -- so capture is structurally absent rather than merely avoided. The alpha predicate is the delicate half and is where the negative tests live: it declines the pointer fast path under a renamed binder (`forall x . P x` vs `forall y . P x`), rejects a right-hand binder capturing a left-hand free symbol, rejects one-sided shadowing (`forall x . forall z . R(x,z)` vs `forall y . forall y . R(y,y)`, which a one-directional correspondence lookup wrongly accepts), and never falls through to structural comparison at odd negation parity, which would claim a formula is its own negation. A symbol occurrence is matched by the binder DEPTH that binds it on each side, never by name and never in one direction only. All six near-misses of the duality were confirmed `sat` by z3 and are pinned as negatives. A 1048-file randomized differential sweep against z3 over quantified UF formulas of this family found 0 disagreements. See docs/mathematics-2026-08/diary-quant-duality.md.",
        "type": "prose"
      },
